<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Hardened Runtime exceptions. Notarisation requires the Hardened Runtime, and
    the Hardened Runtime breaks CPython unless these three are granted. Each one
    is here for a reason, and none of them is a sandbox hole we chose for
    convenience:

    allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory
      CPython and several C extensions map writable-executable memory. Without
      these the interpreter is killed at launch with EXC_BAD_ACCESS, before any
      Chitragupta code runs.

    disable-library-validation
      The bundle loads .so extension modules that were built by their own
      projects and are signed (if at all) by someone other than us. Library
      validation refuses to load any library not signed by the same team ID.

    Deliberately NOT requested:
      * App Sandbox. Chitragupta reads the user's own files, mail and messages by
        design, and runs vendor CLIs the user installed. A sandbox would have to
        be punctured everywhere it mattered, which is worse than being honest
        about being an unsandboxed local tool.
      * com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables. Nothing here
        needs it, and it weakens the runtime.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
